Carafe Lab: two single-layer images match whatever their layer strides. The texture cache compared layer strides
before joining or aliasing overlapping images, and a single-level image the GPU draws into has a layer stride of one
level while the same memory sampled as a texture with a mip chain has a stride of the whole chain. The two never
matched, the texture was filled from guest memory instead of what the GPU drew, and textures a game renders and
samples later, such as NFSU2's road reflection, read black. With one layer there is no other layer to stride to.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/util.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/util.cpp
@@ -1174,6 +1174,10 @@ std::optional<OverlapResult> ResolveOverlap(const ImageInfo& new_info, GPUVAddr
 }
 
 bool IsLayerStrideCompatible(const ImageInfo& lhs, const ImageInfo& rhs) {
+    if (lhs.type != ImageType::e3D && rhs.type != ImageType::e3D && lhs.resources.layers == 1 &&
+        rhs.resources.layers == 1) {
+        return true;
+    }
     // If either of the layer strides is zero, we can assume they are compatible
     // These images generally come from rendertargets
     if (lhs.layer_stride == 0) {
